Lane complete. Committed `e112d7b` on branch `lane-tool-lead-capture`.

**What shipped:**

| File | What |
|---|---|
| `app/api/tools/capture/route.ts` | Server route — origin check, content-type, IP extraction, rate limit (5/hr Upstash, degrades gracefully), honeypot, field validation, type checks. Forwards to `HUB_API_URL/api/public/leads` via `hubFetch` (key server-side only). Validates `tool` is one of six exact slugs. Never exposes the hub key. |
| `components/ToolLeadCapture.tsx` | Client component — name, email, optional company, hidden `_honey`, submit. Loading/success/error states. Result never gated. |
| `lib/rate-limit.ts` | Added `toolCaptureRatelimit()` — 5 per hour, `tool-capture` prefix. |
| `.env.example` | Added `HUB_PUBLIC_API_KEY` placeholder. |

**Wired into all six tools:**

- **ops-health-score** — `12/25 — Fragile: Some Areas Need Work`
- **ai-readiness-check** — `7/10 — Ready: Evaluate with Confidence`
- **automation-roi-calculator** — `150% 3-year ROI — break-even 4 months`
- **downtime-cost-calculator** — `£435/hr downtime cost — £10,440 annual`
- **rto-calculator** — `£12,000/yr saving — £36,000 over 3 years`
- **should-i-replace-erp** — `6/13 — Proceed with Caution`

All summaries use real computed values from each page's existing state — nothing fabricated. `npx tsc --noEmit` passed clean. No new npm dependencies. Not pushed.
